1
00:05:21,818 --> 00:05:27,818
Shut up. Kick-ass.

2
00:10:43,636 --> 00:10:49,636
Kick-Ass is a action, crime film directed by Matthew Vaughn.

3
00:16:05,454 --> 00:16:11,454
Dave Lizewski is an unnoticed high school student and comic book fan who one day decides to become a
super-hero, even though he has no powers, training or meaningful reason to do so.

4
00:21:27,272 --> 00:21:33,272
Dave Lizewski / Kick-Ass, played by Aaron Taylor-Johnson.

5
00:26:49,090 --> 00:26:55,090
Mindy Macready / Hit Girl, played by Chloë Grace Moretz.

6
00:32:10,909 --> 00:32:16,909
Damon Macready / Big Daddy, played by Nicolas Cage.

7
00:37:32,727 --> 00:37:38,727
Katie Deauxma, played by Lyndsy Fonseca.

8
00:42:54,545 --> 00:43:00,545
Frank D'Amico, played by Mark Strong.

9
00:48:16,363 --> 00:48:22,363
Mrs. Zane, played by Deborah Twiss.

10
00:53:38,181 --> 00:53:44,181
Kick-Ass is a 2010 superhero black comedy film directed by Matthew
Vaughn from a screenplay by Jane Goldman and Vaughn.

11
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
It is based on the comic book of the same name by Mark Millar and John
Romita Jr., and is the first film in the Kick-Ass franchise.

12
01:04:21,818 --> 01:04:27,818
It tells the story of an ordinary teenager, Dave Lizewski (Aaron Johnson), who sets
out to become a real-life superhero, calling himself "Kick-Ass".

13
01:09:43,636 --> 01:09:49,636
Dave gets caught up in a bigger fight when he meets Big Daddy (Nicolas Cage), a former cop who, in his quest to bring down the crime boss Frank D'Amico (Mark Strong)
and his son Red Mist (Christopher Mintz-Plasse), has trained his eleven-year-old daughter (Chloë Grace Moretz) to be the ruthless vigilante Hit-Girl.

14
01:15:05,454 --> 01:15:11,454
The film was released in the United Kingdom on 26 March 2010, by Universal
Pictures, and in the United States on 16 April, by Lionsgate.

15
01:20:27,272 --> 01:20:33,272
Despite having generated some controversy for its profanity and strong violence
performed by a child, Kick-Ass was well received by both critics and audiences.

16
01:25:49,090 --> 01:25:55,090
In 2011 it won the Empire Award for Best British Film.

17
01:31:10,909 --> 01:31:16,909
The film has gained a large cult following since its release on DVD and Blu-ray.

18
01:36:32,727 --> 01:36:38,727
A sequel, written and directed by Jeff Wadlow and produced by Vaughn, was released in
August 2013, with Johnson, Mintz-Plasse, and Moretz reprising their roles.

19
01:41:54,545 --> 01:42:00,545
In January 2024, Vaughn announced that a third film, titled Stuntnuts Does School Fight and
directed by Damien Walters, had secretly been greenlit, cast, and had completed filming.

20
01:47:16,363 --> 01:47:22,363
The film explores themes of hero, secret identity,
crime fighter, superhero, dark comedy.

21
01:52:38,181 --> 01:52:44,181
The tone is dark and intense.
